  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a reader, I want the page buttons ‹ › to look the same wherever they show: the arrow is tinted with the accent when a move is possible and greyed when it is not, with no pill filled with the accent colour, so that I see at a glance whether I am on the first or the last page.\n\n### Observed (operator, iPhone, 2026-11-16, build cd049542)\n\n- **Mid-page:** ‹ › share one glass pill, both arrows in the accent.\n- **End of page:** ‹ and › are two separate pills, and the › pill has a **solid accent fill**.\n- Screenshots kept locally by the operator (they show member pseudos, so they are not attached).\n\n### Wanted\n\n- The two separate pills at the end of the page are fine. Keep them.\n- **No solid accent fill** on either pill. Only the **arrow** carries the accent, and only when its move is possible.\n- **‹ greyed on the first page**, **› greyed on the last page**. The same rule applies to the mid-page pill.\n- A greyed arrow is disabled. VoiceOver says « indisponible », and the hit area stays 44 pt or more.\n\n### Scope\n\nThe bottom-bar files (`ReaderBottomBar`, `ReaderPageControls`), together with #961 (the « N / M » bubble in its own centred pill), in one PR under a grouped claim.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] On the first and last pages, the arrows are greyed and disabled; elsewhere, accent and enabled. No solid fill, mid-page or at the end of the page.\n- [ ] A test on the bar state fails without the change (enabled/tint per page position).\n- [ ] Device check in the operator's general review.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
